# XGS Code Review (CR) — description / Objectives text

**Scope:** Use when drafting **Code Review** narrative for **PR/MR**, **Jira Objectives**, **FishEye**, **Crucible**, or similar **post-commit review** fields.  
**Not for:** `git commit` first-line subject / body (see `xgs-git-commit.mdc`).

When the user asks for CR text, **fill or adapt** the template below from the actual branch/JIRA/repro. Keep prose factual; no tool or model attribution in review text.

---

## Template (copy into CR / PR / Objectives)

```markdown
## Linked issues
- XGS-_____ — <short summary>
- Build / image (if relevant): <e.g. 26.1.0.862>

## Summary
<What this change does in one short paragraph.>

## Description
<Problem or requirement; operator-visible impact if any.>

## Root cause (required for crash / intermittent bugs; shorten for pure features)
<Failure mode, evidence gdb `bt` with file:line, broken invariant e.g. RB-tree key mutated in-tree, double remove, UAF, race.>

## Changes
- <Logical change 1>
- <Logical change 2>

## Test plan
1. <Setup: topology, config, versions>
2. <Steps>
3. <Verify: CLI, logs, debug dumps, expected state>
4. <Stress: repeat N× for timing-sensitive issues>

## Risk & rollout
<Risk, mitigation, rollback if any.>

## Review checklist
- [ ] JIRA linked; Objectives align with diff
- [ ] Root cause + invariant stated for crash fixes
- [ ] Test / repro documented with repeat count if intermittent
```

---

## Short form (lightweight CR)

```markdown
**JIRA:** XGS-_____  |  **Build:** ______

**What:** …

**Why / root cause:** …  *(stack + invariant if crash)*

**How:** …

**Test:** …  *(numbered; repeat N× if intermittent)*
```

---

## Reviewer focus — trees, timers, DHCP / protocol-handler

When the diff touches **session tables**, **RB/sorted trees**, **timers**, or **aging paths**:

- **RB / sort keys:** No in-place change of the **key field** while the node remains in the tree; prefer **RB_REMOVE → update key → RB_INSERT** (or equivalent).
- **Identity fields:** No `memcpy`/overwrite of **MAC/chaddr** (or other tree keys) while the node is still in the **hardware-address** tree unless the code removes and reinserts correctly **with locking**.
- **Intermittent cores:** Require **numbered repro**, **stress repeats** (e.g. ≥5×), and debug commands that prove structure consistency (e.g. session dump + Fwd RB dump — substitute per subsystem).
- Reject fixes that only mask null derefs **without** explaining why the pointer is invalid.

---

## Mapping to typical Jira CR fields

| Field / section | Fill from template |
|-----------------|-------------------|
| Description | **Description** |
| Objectives | **Summary** + **Changes** |
| Root cause / analysis.gp | **Root cause** |
| Test / verification | **Test plan** |

Do not duplicate the entire git commit body into CR; CR should carry **reviewer-oriented** context, repro, and risk.
